          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Search for and verify these two key papers cited in an information extraction proposal:\n\n1. **UniNER (ICLR 2024, arXiv 2308.03279)**: The claim is that UniNER demonstrated per-type individual queries outperform all-in-one batch queries by 3.3 F1 points. Also that UniNER-13B achieved 43.4% avg F1. Verify these specific numbers.\n\n2. **LLM-PEE (EMNLP 2025 Main, arXiv 2503.02628)**: \"Towards Event Extraction with Massive Types: LLM-based Collaborative Annotation and Partitioning Extraction.\" The claim is it uses ColBERT retrieval to recall top-k types, then confidence-based partitioning into groups, achieving 60.2% TC F1 on EEMT dataset (+5.4 over KnowCoder). The claim is that it handles 3,465 event types. Verify these numbers.\n\nUse WebSearch and WebFetch if needed. Under 250 words."
            }
          ],
